नवानि गृह्णाति नरोऽपराणि ।
तथा शरीराणि विहाय जीर्णा-
न्यन्यानि संयाति नवानि देही ॥ २२ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":609,\"bb\":553,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/22/b553/\",\"body_value\":\"vāsāṁsi jīrṇāni yathā vihāya
navāni gṛhṇāti naro ’parāṇi
tathā śarīrāṇi vihāya jīrṇāny
anyāni saṁyāti navāni dehī\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":610,\"bb\":554,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/22/b554/\",\"shadow_value\":\"vāsāṁsi – garments; jīrṇāni – old and worn out; yathā – just as; vihāya – giving up; navāni – new garments; gṛhṇāti – does accept; naraḥ – a man; aparāṇi – others; tathā – in the same way; śarīrāṇi – bodies; vihāya – giving up; jirṇāni – old and useless; anyāni – different; saṁyāti – verily accepts; navāni – new sets; dehī – the embodied.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"vāsāṁsi\",\"translation\":\"garments\"},{\"word\":\"jīrṇāni\",\"translation\":\"old and worn out\"},{\"word\":\"yathā\",\"translation\":\"just as\"},{\"word\":\"vihāya\",\"translation\":\"giving up\"},{\"word\":\"navāni\",\"translation\":\"new garments\"},{\"word\":\"gṛhṇāti\",\"translation\":\"does accept\"},{\"word\":\"naraḥ\",\"translation\":\"a man\"},{\"word\":\"aparāṇi\",\"translation\":\"others\"},{\"word\":\"tathā\",\"translation\":\"in the same way\"},{\"word\":\"śarīrāṇi\",\"translation\":\"bodies\"},{\"word\":\"vihāya\",\"translation\":\"giving up\"},{\"word\":\"jirṇāni\",\"translation\":\"old and useless\"},{\"word\":\"anyāni\",\"translation\":\"different\"},{\"word\":\"saṁyāti\",\"translation\":\"verily accepts\"},{\"word\":\"navāni\",\"translation\":\"new sets\"},{\"word\":\"dehī\",\"translation\":\"the embodied\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":611,\"bb\":555,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/22/b555/\",\"body_value\":\"As a person puts on new garments, giving up old ones, the soul similarly accepts new material bodies, giving up the old and useless ones.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":612,\"bb\":556,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/22/b556/\",\"body_value\":\"Change of body by the atomic individual soul is an accepted fact. Even the modern scientists who do not believe in the existence of the soul, but at the same time cannot explain the source of energy from the heart, have to accept continuous changes of body which appear from childhood to boyhood and from boyhood to youth and again from youth to old age. From old age, the change is transferred to another body. This has already been explained in a previous verse (2.13).\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":613,\"bb\":557,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/22/b557/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":614,\"bb\":558,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/22/b558/\",\"body_value\":\"samāne vṛkṣe puruṣo nimagno
’nīśayā śocati muhyamānaḥ
juṣṭaṁ yadā paśyaty anyam īśam
asya mahimānam iti vīta-śokaḥ\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":615,\"bb\":559,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/22/b559/\",\"body_value\":\"“Although the two birds are in the same tree, the eating bird is fully engrossed with anxiety and moroseness as the enjoyer of the fruits of the tree. But if in some way or other he turns his face to his friend the Lord and knows His glories – at once the suffering bird becomes free from all anxieties.” Arjuna has now turned his face towards his eternal friend, Kṛṣṇa, and is understanding the Bhagavad-gītā from Him. And thus, hearing from Kṛṣṇa, he can understand the supreme glories of the Lord and be free from lamentation.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":616,\"bb\":560,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/22/b560/\",\"body_value\":\"Arjuna is advised herewith by the Lord not to lament for the bodily change of his old grandfather and his teacher. He should rather be happy to kill their bodies in the righteous fight so that they may be cleansed at once of all reactions from various bodily activities. One who lays down his life on the sacrificial altar, or in the proper battlefield, is at once cleansed of bodily reactions and promoted to a higher status of life. So there was no cause for Arjuna’s lamentation.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 2.22\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 2.22\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chu